# Every text file is stored AND checked out with LF, on every platform. The hooks, the kernel and
# their installed-layout tests do byte-level content surgery on real installed copies; a checkout
# that materializes CRLF (autocrlf's default on Windows) makes those mutations silently no-op, and
# the suites' own vacuity guards fail the run — correctly. One line ending everywhere is the fix,
# not looser mutations.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored official reference texts — always binary, never line-ending-converted.
# (without this, a PDF whose early bytes lack NULs could be misclassified as text
#  and corrupted on checkout.)
*.pdf binary
